# EVERY pin lives here. Renovate bumps this file. NOTHING may say `latest`.
#
# The registry is the in-cluster GitLab registry (docs/environment.md). Harbor is
# NOT deployed; zot is a pull-through cache only.
REGISTRY=registry.orac.local/agentic/gonk-project

# The image tag. NEVER `latest`. `make images`/`make push` set it from the git
# SHA (see Makefile: GONK_TAG ?= $(GONK_VERSION)-$(shell git rev-parse --short=12 HEAD)).
GONK_VERSION=v0.1.0

# --- OD-3: settled (Task 5) ---------------------------------------------------
# opencode-ai 1.18.3, verified real (npm dist-tags "latest" == 1.18.3 as of
# 2026-07-16; github.com/anomalyco/opencode release v1.18.3 exists with a
# published linux-x64 static binary, sha256 checksummed below in
# Dockerfile.agent). No owner preference was recorded, so this pins "whatever
# is current at execution time" per OD-3's own fallback -- record it in
# ADR-004 (Task 9).  A floating opencode is an agent whose behaviour changes
# under you, and spec 11.4's NAMED RISK (ACP session resume across pod
# recreation) is version-sensitive: pin exact, bump deliberately.
OPENCODE_VERSION=1.18.3

# go.mod says `go 1.26`; PLAN.md's CI notes pin 1.26.2 alongside
# golangci-lint:v2.12.2 (go1.26.2) so local and CI cannot disagree -- carried
# here too. Digest resolved 2026-07-16 (Docker-Content-Digest header on the
# tag's manifest-list, not guessed): a tag can move, a digest cannot, and
# Task 7's `TestBaseImagesArePinnedByDigest` gate will check this.
#
# BUMPED to 1.26.5 in Task 6 (Plan 04): gascity's own go.mod, AT THE EXACT
# GASCITY_REF SHA PINNED BELOW, requires `go >= 1.26.5` -- Dockerfile.controller's
# `gc` build stage failed outright against 1.26.2 ("go.mod requires go >= 1.26.5;
# running go 1.26.2"), a real, reproduced build failure, not a hypothetical one.
# 1.26.5 still satisfies gonk's own `go 1.26` directive (go.mod has no upper
# bound), so this is a safe shared bump across every Dockerfile stage AND the
# local dev-box toolchain (which is already 1.26.5 -- `go version` on this box).
# Digest resolved 2026-07-16 the same way as before (Docker-Content-Digest on
# the docker.io/library/golang:1.26.5 tag's manifest-list).
GO_VERSION=1.26.5@sha256:ae5a2316d12f3e78fd99177dad452e6ad4f240af2d71d57b480c3477f250fec6

# GLAB_VERSION / BD_VERSION are release TAGS (gitlab.com/gitlab-org/cli and
# github.com/gastownhall/beads), each with a verified sha256 in
# Dockerfile.agent's install steps -- a tag alone is not the pin, the tag +
# checksum together are.
# GLAB_VERSION IS NO LONGER CONSUMED BY ANY IMAGE (gonk-0de, 2026-08-18): glab
# was removed from the agent, which was its only user, because the broker model
# leaves that pod with no forge credential for it to use. Kept, commented, so
# the checksummed version is at hand if a credentialed tool is ever justified --
# and so nobody reads a live-looking pin as evidence that glab still ships.
# GLAB_VERSION=1.108.0
# BUMPED 1.0.3 -> 1.1.0 for gonk-fsl: the controller's `gc init` (exec:gc-beads-bd
# lifecycle) refuses a store whose bd is older than 1.0.4 -- reproduced in
# chart/gonk/smoke/gc-controller-smoke.md ("bundled bd is v1.0.3 while gc init
# wants v1.0.4+"). 1.1.0 is exactly what gascity's own deps.env pins at the
# GASCITY_REF below (BD_VERSION=v1.1.0), so this tracks upstream rather than
# guessing. Shared pin: BOTH Dockerfile.agent and Dockerfile.controller read it,
# and both carry the matching sha256 (b0f3dd60...) in their bd fetch step.
BD_VERSION=1.1.0               # beads (MIT); gascity deps.env pins v1.1.0 at GASCITY_REF
GASCITY_REF=4fda5a28445f42d6e789fc7f5751645ac4fecd19  # the SHA recorded in Task 4 Step 1

# DOLT_VERSION: the Dolt CLI the controller's exec:gc-beads-bd provider shells
# out to (dolt sql / dolt sql-server) to inspect and initialize the city's beads
# store. WITHOUT it, gc-beads-bd reports "managed Dolt server unreachable" and
# `gc init` fails (gonk-fsl). 2.1.7 is the exact pin in gascity's deps.env AND
# .github/scripts/install-dolt-archive.sh at GASCITY_REF; the linux-amd64 sha256
# below is the one that install script hard-codes, re-verified here by download.
# Fetched by URL (github.com/dolthub/dolt/releases) in Dockerfile.controller's
# checksum-verified fetch stage -- the tag + this sha256 together are the pin.
# tarball: dolt-linux-amd64.tar.gz -> dolt-linux-amd64/bin/dolt
DOLT_VERSION=2.1.7             # dolt CLI (Apache-2.0); sha256 15983e81...477e28e7 (linux-amd64)

# Base runtime image, pinned by DIGEST the same way (Docker-Content-Digest on
# the tag's manifest-list, resolved 2026-07-16).
DEBIAN_BASE=debian:trixie-slim@sha256:020c0d20b9880058cbe785a9db107156c3c75c2ac944a6aa7ab59f2add76a7bd

# --- Task 7 (Plan 04): gonk-intake / gonk-meter -------------------------------
# Distroless runtime for the two pure-Go server binaries (no apt packages
# needed at runtime -- unlike Dockerfile.agent/.controller, neither ships a
# shelled-out tool). Pinned by DIGEST the same way as DEBIAN_BASE
# (Docker-Content-Digest header on the tag's manifest-list, resolved
# 2026-07-16, verified reachable and pullable with `podman pull` from this
# box -- gcr.io is not blocked here, unlike registry.orac.local itself for the
# other direction).
DISTROLESS_BASE=gcr.io/distroless/static-debian12:nonroot@sha256:aef9602f8710ec12bde19d593fed1f76c708531bb7aba205110f1029786ead7b
